---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DayQuiz from '../components/DayQuiz.astro';
import BreadcrumbList from '../../vendor/site-toolkit/packages/schema/src/BreadcrumbList.astro';
import { jsonLdStringify } from '../../vendor/site-toolkit/packages/schema/src/jsonLdStringify';
import { dayQuizItems } from '../data/dayQuiz';
import { SITE_ORIGIN, SITE_TITLE, AUTHOR_NAME } from '../consts';

const pageUrl = `${SITE_ORIGIN}/true-or-false/`;
const title = 'True or False? A DayAlmanac Observance Quiz';
const description =
	'Pull a claim from our own observance, birthstone, and zodiac coverage. Is this day really an official holiday, is it really the same as that other day? Guess whether it holds up, before you see the documented answer.';
const updated = '2026-08-06';

const articleCount = new Set(dayQuizItems.map((i) => i.sourceSlug)).size;

const webAppSchema = jsonLdStringify({
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'WebApplication',
	name: 'True or False? DayAlmanac Quiz',
	url: pageUrl,
	description,
	applicationCategory: 'EducationApplication',
	operatingSystem: 'Any',
	browserRequirements: 'Requires JavaScript',
	offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
	publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE_TITLE, url: `${SITE_ORIGIN}/` },
	dateModified: updated,
});

const breadcrumbItems = [
	{ name: 'Home', item: `${SITE_ORIGIN}/` },
	{ name: 'True or False?', item: pageUrl },
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
	<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={webAppSchema} slot="head" is:inline />
	<BreadcrumbList slot="head" items={breadcrumbItems} />

	<div class="mx-auto max-w-[680px]">
		<nav class="mb-8 text-sm text-[var(--ink)]/40">
			<a href="/" class="no-underline hover:text-[var(--ink)] hover:underline">Home</a>
			<span class="mx-1.5">/</span>
			<span class="text-[var(--ink)]/70">True or False?</span>
		</nav>

		<h1 class="font-display m-0 text-[2.1rem] leading-tight font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">{title}</h1>
		<p class="mt-3 text-[1.05rem] leading-relaxed text-[var(--ink)]/70">{description}</p>
		<p class="mt-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-[var(--ink)]/40">Last updated {updated}</p>

		<div class="panel mt-7 rounded-[10px] px-6 py-5">
			<p class="rubric m-0">Core summary</p>
			<p class="mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-[var(--ink)]/85">
				Every claim here is pulled verbatim from the FAQ section of a real DayAlmanac article. Nothing is
				invented for the quiz. Each round draws 12 claims at random from a deck of {dayQuizItems.length},
				spanning {articleCount} different articles, so the set changes each time you play. Pick "True" or
				"False," then read the sourced explanation and follow the link back to the full story.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="mt-8">
			<DayQuiz count={12} />
		</div>

		<article class="font-prose mt-9 text-[0.9375rem] leading-[1.85] text-[var(--ink)]/80">
			<h2 class="font-display mt-10 mb-3 text-[1.4rem] font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">Why a quiz instead of a list of facts</h2>
			<p class="mb-3.5">
				A page that just states "no, National Cat Day and International Cat Day are not the same observance"
				can be read and repeated by an AI answer box in a single sentence, so the visitor never needs to open
				the page. A claim you have to judge for yourself, before the verdict and its sourcing appear, doesn't
				work that way: it needs a click and a guess first. The underlying facts are the same ones already
				published across this site's <a href="/" class="text-[var(--flag-dark)] no-underline hover:underline">observance, birthstone, and zodiac coverage</a>;
				this page just turns a sample of them into a game.
			</p>
			<p class="mb-0">
				Every explanation links back to the article it came from, with the same sourcing already cited
				there. Nothing on this page is asserted without a documented origin in the linked piece.
			</p>
		</article>

		<div class="mt-10 flex items-start gap-4 border-t border-[var(--rule)] pt-6">
			<div>
				<p class="m-0 font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]"><a href="/about/" class="no-underline text-inherit hover:text-[var(--flag-dark)]">{AUTHOR_NAME}</a></p>
				<p class="rubric mt-1 mb-0">Editor, {SITE_TITLE}</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>
